r UCDBase and transfer-learning models achieve comparable or superior performance on in-silico mixture deconvolution to existing, reference-based, state-of-the-art methods. Feature attribute analysis uncovers gene signatures associated with cell-type specific inflammatory-fibrotic responses in ischemic kidney injury, discerns cancer subtypes, and accurately deconvolves tumor microenvironments. UCD identifies pathologic changes in cell fractions among bulk-RNA-Seq data for several disease states. Applied to lung cancer scRNA-Seq data, UCD annotates and distinguishes normal from cancerous cells. Overall, UCD enhances transcriptomic data analysis, aiding in assessment of cellular and spatial context.", "affiliation": "Department of Genetics and Genomic Sciences, Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, NY, USA.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "F30 CA265288", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIAMS NIH HHS", "acronym": "AR", "grantId": "P30 AR079200", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIGMS NIH HHS", "acronym": "GM", "grantId": "T32 GM146636", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Gene Expression Profiling", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Sequence Analysis, RNA", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Single-Cell Analysis", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Transcriptome"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "RNA-Seq", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifie